  "text": "مياه AssemblyCompany>\nSectionsInebCompany\nHere is the solution for the problem of sequence consisting of integers, each successive term is obtained by addition of numbers 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 to the previous term, except to be not divisible by 3, 7 and 11 respectively, before we come across a one divisible by 3, 7 or 11,\n    First integer of the sequence (N1)=2\n    Second integer in the sequence ( N2)=2+1=3\n    Third integer in the sequence ( N3)=3+2=5\n    Fourth integer in the sequence ( N4)=3+3=6\n    Fifth integer in the sequence ( N5)=5+5=10\n    Now, we come across a number divisible by 3, 7 or 11 respectively at N6=10+3=8\n    Hence, only 5 terms of the sequence are possible as per the given condition. Please correct me if I've made any mistake in this problem, Abhishek.\nمراجـاجـب : والله لم يكن ليلا على هذا المهمه :(",
